  "body": "# Desktop Pet v0.4.5 release notes\n\n## Authorized corrective boundary\n\nCore **v0.4.5** and the genuine **legacy v0.3.10** envelope are the separately authorized correction for retained migration history blocking later native checks. No v0.4.5/v0.3.10 publication or runtime acceptance is claimed by this source ledger before actual release evidence is recorded. Earlier tags, Release bodies, assets, frozen v0.3.6 matched pair and beta formula remain immutable. Herdr integration **v0.4.1**, exact `6d2ac0446f6ecb84f179e21fac3c5b02e07dc8e8`, release `412252863`, assets `[]`, remains the retirement authority. There is no new Herdr or Tern integration tag.\n\nNeutral identity remains protocol **4**, observation **2**, integration API **1**. The same common source compiles the genuine bounded v0.3.10 legacy executable/helper/bundle with protocol **3**, observation **1**, integration API **1**; it is not a renamed neutral app. Existing adapter/contracts revisions and scoped generated-app ownership admission remain unchanged.\n\n## Retained history versus fresh execution authority\n\nActual public Core v0.4.2-to-v0.4.3 ordinary standalone update completed on the original legacy profile. The next public v0.4.3 native Check displayed `Migration history: migration requires approved neutral stable 0.4.3 release` while reading completed v0.4.2 migration `c66961f9e5a91c0023545065ae61385b`. Published v0.4.4 retained the same validation defect. That blocked public checker did not complete a v0.4.3-to-v0.4.4 update.\n\nThe correction separates read-only historical structure validation from current-version execution authorization. Historical lookup retains bounded owned/private reads, schema, authority, canonical profile/image scope, evidence names and the original plan SHA binding. A completed older migration for a different newer running image does not obstruct its ordinary Check. An older Unknown record remains observable only in its original scope and is never replayed, cleared, reset or promoted into fresh authority. All fresh plan reads, writes, execution, startup and resume continue to require the exact current compiled approved neutral stable release.\n\nTwo regressions failed before the fix with the exact current-version rejection; all **70** coordinator tests then passed. A throwaway probe built against the changed coordinator ran in the disposable VM against the actual original v0.4.2 plan and still-running public v0.4.3 image: lookup returned no matching historical operation for that newer image, while fresh old-plan read remained rejected. All original configuration and **321** state-file hashes and the original ready PID/instance were unchanged. This is working-library qualification, not proof of a repaired published binary. Evidence: `actual-core043-history042-working-fix-readonly-smoke.json`; failing-before `artifact://1892`, passing-after `artifact://1894`.\n\n## Independently observed previous release acceptance\n\nThe [v0.4.4 ledger](https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/blob/v0.4.5/docs/releases/v0.4.4.md) retains the completed genuine public managed v0.3.6 Check/A-to-v0.3.9 and separate B-to-v0.4.4 proof, exact old profile, genuine immutable Herdr refresh and unrelated default preservation. It does not establish new v0.3.10/v0.4.5 acceptance. Original immutable v0.3.8 B preparation failure and earlier Unknown evidence are not rewritten by successor success.\n\nActual public v0.3.9's beta route was exercised separately with the original anonymous protocol-2 beta archive: SHA-256 `d49824778dc0d898b4386cc04a4fbed34da40ebfe990148441d365984555d1aa`. Its installer rejected replacement while the owned beta was live, then rejected direct bridge installation after explicit Stop. The shipped `install-0.3.6.sh --legacy-stopped` installed the original frozen matched pair, archive SHA-256 `5d40f6ada23f7d91d967a98331b28ea767202f5d01b7cd7732b2d9e543fdaafa`, without autostart. Explicit Start reached genuine v0.3.6 UI/control readiness on the exact beta config/state. Both original beta and new v0.3.6 helpers remained strictly signed; all 38 non-app source/Git/user files, tracked/untracked source edits, beta profile and unrelated Core profile hashes were preserved. The owned v0.3.6 was explicitly stopped after proof. Beta formula SHA-256 remained `6794910b429160df72db412e5bc2923ec31c65838776bffa0e8dba83f0d7f070`. Evidence: `beta-public039-pinned036-real-matched-pair-source-profile-preservation.json` and `beta-public039-pinned036-completed-owned-app-stopped.json`. These are v0.3.9 entrypoint observations, not a claimed later tag run.\n\n## Independent external prerequisites\n\nGenuine Tern's supported owned window could not open normal macOS keychain sign-in. Genuine OMP remained at provider sign-in/NoModel, without an interactive-ready agent or real prompt completion. Both real SDK connection orders, actual prompt/transcript completion and explicit Tern reconnect remain unproved; no credentials, fake backend or ACK substitute is used.\n\nCore v0.4.4's Linux Wiki job rendered all **38** managed pages, then failed because dedicated `WIKI_PUBLISH_TOKEN` is missing. Wiki owner initialization and dedicated publication credentials remain external prerequisites; no broad token fallback or successful public Wiki write is claimed.\n"
}
